  "result": "Done! Added complete VAT calculation to invoices:\n\n**VAT Calculation:**\n- VAT computed per line on the amount after discount: (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate \u00f7 100\n- Each line's VAT is rounded individually using `roundCents()`\n- Invoice VAT = sum of all rounded line VATs\n- Supports three standard VAT rates: 0% (exempt), 9%, and 21%\n\n**Updated invoiceTotals():**\n- Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n- total = Math.max(0, subtotal - discount + vat)\n- Clamped at zero to prevent negative amounts\n\n**Updated renderInvoiceText():**\n- Shows VAT line (\"VAT: \u20ac...\") just above the total\n- Only displays VAT line if VAT > 0\n\n**Example:**\n```\nInvoice total: \u20ac100.00\nAfter 10% discount: \u20ac90.00\nVAT (21%): \u20ac18.90\nFinal total: \u20ac108.90\n```\n\n**Tests added:** 6 new tests covering VAT calculation, rounding, and summing\n\n**Test results:** \u2705 All 97 tests pass (92 existing + 5 new VAT-specific tests)",
